# Agent coordination and token budget

Canonical spec: `docs/architecture/modeling-operator-specification.md`.
Active work: `docs/coordination/CURRENT-MILESTONE.md`, `docs/coordination/TASK-BOARD.md`, `tasks/`.
Generated indexes: `generated/repo-map.md`, `generated/public-api-index.md`, `generated/package-graph.md`, `generated/test-index.md`.

Cursor owns architecture, planning, review, and integration. Antigravity owns one bounded task packet at a time. Do not install CrewAI, AutoGPT, or Aider.

## Retrieval

1. Read the active task packet before exploring code.
2. Open only the specification sections cited by that task.
3. Use Serena symbol lookup (when the MCP server is connected) before opening whole files.
4. Use `rg` for exact text and filenames.
5. Read generated repository/API indexes before scanning packages.
6. Never read `dist`, coverage, source maps, large fixtures, or generated bundles.
7. Never read all workspace packages for a single-package task.
8. Generate a targeted Repomix bundle only when symbol lookup is insufficient: `pnpm repo:context -- --preset <name> --budget <n>`. Presets include `mesh`, `snapping`, `transform`, `commands-history`, `input-tools`.
9. Stay inside the preset token budget (default 15k–25k). Prefer paths, symbol names, requirement IDs, diffs, and commits over pasted source.
10. Store decisions in ADRs or existing architecture docs. Do not re-argue resolved items.

## Execution

11. Run targeted package tests during implementation.
12. Run the full suite only at integration (`pnpm check:release` or `pnpm test` + `pnpm typecheck`).
13. Do not send Antigravity a broad goal such as “complete the UV system.”
14. Limit Antigravity to one vertical slice and the task’s allowed-file list.
15. Cursor reviews every Antigravity change before integration.
16. Antigravity cannot add dependencies or change frozen contracts (`docs/coordination/API-FREEZE.md`).
17. No completion claim without recorded test evidence.
18. Cursor and Antigravity must not edit the same files concurrently. Branches: `integration/release-1` vs `agent/<TASK-ID>`.
19. Validate packets with `pnpm check:agent -- --task tasks/<ID>.md --changed-files …`.
20. Refresh Serena’s index after large edits; do not treat the index as newer than the working tree.

## Branches

- Cursor integrates on `integration/release-1` once that branch exists.
- Antigravity works only on `agent/<TASK-ID>`.
- Communication protocol is task files + handoff reports in `tasks/TEMPLATE.md`, not chat memory.
